---@class boat_dev.ForkSandboxRequest
---@field sandboxId string Public Sandbox id returned by create/list/get sandbox calls.
---@field idempotencyKey? string Optional exactly-once key for creating a sandbox. Send your own opaque, account-unique value (a UUID) to make `POST /sandboxes` safe to retry when the response is lost (network timeout, 5xx): the first request creates the sandbox and binds it to the key; every later request with the **same account, key, and request body** returns that same sandbox instead of creating a second, billable one. Behavior: keys are retained for **24 hours**; a concurrent or early retry while the first sandbox is still being minted returns `409` `idempotency_in_progress` (retry shortly, same key); reusing a key with a **different body** returns `409` `idempotency_key_reused`; timeouts and 5xx are safe to retry with the same key; a create that fails before the sandbox exists releases the key within ~2 minutes so a retry can create the sandbox. Omit the header to keep the default (non-idempotent) behavior.
---@field labels? boat_dev.ForkSandboxRequestLabelsMap Labels of the fork. The fork never takes the source's labels. Same rules as `CreateSandboxRequest.labels`.
---@field failFast? boolean Pass `true` to fork only if a machine is ready right now. Within about 1.5 s you get the usual `202`, or `503` `no_ready_machine` with no fork created and nothing counted against your start limits.
---@field monitoring? boolean `false` creates the fork with monitoring off: Boat keeps no command or process output, process list or CPU/RAM samples for it. Omitted, the fork keeps the source sandbox's setting. `true` turns it on for the fork, unless the account has monitoring off by default (`409` `monitoring_off_for_account`).
---@field env? boat_dev.ForkSandboxRequestEnvMap Replaces the env the fork would otherwise inherit from the source sandbox. Same validation rules as `CreateSandboxRequest.env`.
---@field environment? string Optionally pin the fork to a different named sandbox environment. Omit to inherit the source sandbox's environment. Unknown names are rejected with `unknown_environment`.
---@field noEnv? boolean Make the fork no-env (see `CreateSandboxRequest.noEnv`). A fork of a no-env sandbox is always no-env regardless of this field.
---@field type? boat_dev.ForkSandboxRequestType|string Machine size for the fork. Omit to inherit the source sandbox's type. `xlarge` needs the $100/month plan or higher (403 `machine_class_plan_required`). The source sandbox is never modified. Shrinking is rejected with `type_too_small` when the source's data would not fit the smaller disk.
---@field ttlSeconds? number|distilled.Null Auto-stop for the fork, in seconds. Omit for the 1 hour default; the fork does NOT inherit the source sandbox's TTL, so forking a sandbox that has auto-stop disabled still gives you a fork that stops itself. `null` disables auto-stop, which means nothing will ever stop this sandbox for you.

