---Recover a sandbox that stopped responding
---
---Power-cycle the machine of a sandbox that stopped answering. The disk is not
---touched. The sandbox usually answers again within 1-2 minutes and then saves
---your work by itself; `sandbox.recovered` fires when it does.
---
---Refused with `409`:
---- `sandbox_is_reachable`: the sandbox answers normally.
---- `too_soon`: a recover started less than 10 minutes ago.
---- `no_machine`: the sandbox has no machine. Resume it instead.
---- `recover_unsupported`: its machine cannot be power-cycled. Wait for it to
---  answer, or stop it with `{"force": true}` and resume it from its last
---  good snapshot. With no snapshot, a forced stop loses everything.
---- `reset_failed`: the power-cycle failed. Reply to the incident email.
---
---`POST /sandboxes/{sandboxId}/recover`
---Errors: NotFound, Conflict, SandboxIsReachable, RecoverTooSoon, SandboxHasNoMachine, RecoverUnsupported, RecoverResetFailed.
---@param input boat_dev.RecoverSandboxRequest
---@return boat_dev.RecoverSandboxResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:recover_sandbox(input) end

