---Share sandbox with the organization
---
---Let every member of the organization that pays for this sandbox use it.
---
---A sandbox that holds none of your personal logins is shared at once.
---
---A sandbox that holds them: your personal logins (GitHub token, Claude and Codex logins,
---environment secrets, the sandbox's own CLI key) are never pushed to it again and are
---wiped off its disk at its next start, so a teammate never acts as you. Files you wrote
---stay. The wipe is one-way: the sandbox stays like a `noEnv` sandbox from then on. A
---running sandbox stays `view` for the organization until you stop and resume it
---(`restartRequired`): its running programs hold your logins in memory.
---
---Teammates never read history recorded before the share.
---
---Only the person who created the sandbox can share it, and only a sandbox billed to
---an organization. Sharing an already shared sandbox is a no-op. Undo with
---`POST /sandboxes/{sandboxId}/unshare`.
---
---`POST /sandboxes/{sandboxId}/share`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input boat_dev.ShareSandboxRequest
---@return boat_dev.ShareSandboxResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:share_sandbox(input) end

---Steer a running turn
---
---Send a new message to a turn that is already running, without losing what the agent is doing. This is what typing into a coding agent while it works does: the instruction is taken into account and the work continues.
---
---Where the harness has a native mid-turn primitive (Claude Code, Codex, pi, Prime Agent) nothing is interrupted and the response has `native: true`. Where it does not (OpenCode), Boat interrupts that turn and immediately continues the SAME conversation with the instruction, keeping the session and its memory, and the response has `native: false`.
---
---Refused with **409 `no_running_turn`** when the conversation has nothing in flight; queue work with `POST /prompt` instead. `error.details.reason` says why: `turn_ended` (with `error.details.lastTurn.status` and `.error` of the newest turn), `turn_not_started` (the turn is starting; retry in a moment), `no_turn`, `not_running` (the sandbox is not running) or `delivery_failed` (the sandbox did not accept the steer; check the turn before sending more work). The steer shows up in `GET /events` as a `steer` event. See [Integrated agents](/integrated-agents).
---
---`POST /sandboxes/{sandboxId}/steer`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict, NoRunningTurn.
---@param input boat_dev.SteerSandboxRequest
---@return boat_dev.SteerSandboxResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:steer_sandbox(input) end

---Stop a detached command
---
---Sends SIGTERM to the command and every process it started, then SIGKILL to what is left after 5 s. Only a process started with `detached` can be stopped. The response carries the command's history record with its final state and output.
---
---`DELETE /sandboxes/{sandboxId}/commands/{processId}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict, SandboxNotRunning.
---@param input boat_dev.StopCommandRequest
---@return boat_dev.StopCommandResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:stop_command(input) end

---Stop and archive sandbox
---
---Stop active work and archive/snapshot the sandbox for later resume or fork.
---
---A stop always saves the sandbox's disk first. If that save is failing, the stop is
---refused and the sandbox keeps running so your work is not discarded, we retry
---automatically and email you. You are not billed for time spent in that state.
---
---The stop is an operation: the response and the sandbox carry it as `stop`, with an
---`id` and a `status`. Poll `GET /sandboxes/{sandboxId}` until `stop.status` is
---`completed`. A failed attempt shows `failing` with its `error` and is retried
---until the sandbox archives; commands and prompts you send meanwhile do not cancel
---it. Only a resume ends it early (`superseded`). Calling stop again while one is
---pending returns the same `id`.
---
---Set `force: true` to stop anyway, keeping the last successful snapshot and
---losing everything written since then. This is irreversible; only reach for it
---after a stop has already failed. A force on a stop that is already pending
---escalates that stop.
---
---`POST /sandboxes/{sandboxId}/stop`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, SandboxAlreadyStopped.
---@param input boat_dev.StopSandboxRequest
---@return boat_dev.StopSandboxResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:stop_sandbox(input) end

